### Test Discrepancy Note (§2c)

- **Scenario A** ([`Craft.test.js:365`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Craft.test.js#L365)): `assert.strictEqual(craft.ns, 1)` (actual `0`, expected `1`):
  - **Reason**: In Java's [`Craft.java`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/decompilation/java-src/Craft.java), constructor sets `this.ns = 0` and `this.nd = 0`. `preform()` never mutates `ns` or `nd` (only `dosmokes()` does), and `reset()` does not touch them. In [`CraftProbe.java`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/tools/CraftProbe.java), a single `craft` instance was reused across test sections; `dosmokes()` in section 5 incremented `ns` and `nd` to `1` prior to Scenario A in section 6. [`Craft.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Craft.test.js) instantiated a fresh `new Craft(m)` for Scenario A without calling `dosmokes()`, yet asserted the probe's residual values `craft.ns = 1` and `craft.nd = 1`.
  - Per §2c, [`Craft.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Craft.test.js) was left untouched.

